{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Its crop.</b> The place of the excrement — this is the זֶפֶק (Sifra)." "<b>With its feathers.</b> With the entrails' contents; and נוֹצָה is a term for something repulsive, as in ״כִּי נָצוּ גַּם נָעוּ״ (Lamentations 4) — and this is what Onkelos translates בְּאוּכְלֵהּ; and this is the midrash of Abba Yosi ben Chanan, who said: he takes the crop with it. And our Rabbis of blessed memory said: he cuts around the זֶפֶק with a knife in the shape of a window-frame and takes it with the feathers that are on the skin (Sifra). In the cattle burnt offering, which eats only from its owner's trough, it says ״וְהַקֶּרֶב וְהַכְּרָעַיִם יִרְחַץ בַּמַּיִם וְהִקְטִיר״; but the bird, which feeds from robbery, it says ״וְהִשְׁלִיךְ אֶת הַמֵּעַיִם״ — because it ate from robbery (Leviticus Rabbah 3)." "<b>Next to the altar on the east side.</b> On the east side of the ramp (Sifra)." "<b>To the place of the ash.</b> The place where they deposit the terumah of the ash every morning and the sweeping-clean of the inner altar and the menorah — and all of them are absorbed there in their place."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:42.573061881Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}